# LedgerProof AI

LedgerProof AI helps tax associates turn client facts into
evidence-supported draft tax memos with clear professional-review flags.

## Intended User

Tax associates at regional CPA firms with 50–200 employees who prepare
client tax memos and supporting workpapers for manager or partner review.

## First Working Slice

A user loads one of two fictional client scenarios and selects
“Generate Draft Memo.”

The complete-facts example displays a provisional memo with client facts,
a purchase-total calculation, sample evidence references, and items
requiring professional review.

The missing-facts example displays clarification questions.
Blank inputs receive a validation message. Unsupported inputs receive
an explanation of the demo’s coverage.

## Open the Prototype

Prototype link: REPLACE_WITH_WORKING_REPLIT_LINK

Load an example, select “Generate Draft Memo,” and inspect the result.
Use “Edit Input / Try Again” to return to the input.

## AI Role and Prototype Status

The future AI system would research authoritative guidance, synthesize
client documents, prepare and revise draft memos, identify missing facts,
and route uncertain judgments for professional review.

This milestone uses a Wizard-of-Oz prototype. Drafting, research, and
judgment routing are simulated through prepared responses.

The interface, example loading, input validation, result display, and
retry flow work. No live AI model or authoritative-source search is
connected. Sample evidence is fictional, and the review checklist is
not tax authority.

## Test Results

| Test | Input or action | What happened | Pass, partial, or fail |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Typical | Loaded complete example and generated draft | Not run | Pending |
| Challenge | Loaded missing-facts example and generated | Not run | Pending |
| Invalid or empty | Submitted blank input | Not run | Pending |

## Known Limitations

1. **Prepared scenarios only.** The prototype supports two fictional
   examples. A future version would analyze user-supplied facts
   and documents.

2. **No live research or tax determination.** Sources and drafting are
   simulated, and tax treatment remains unresolved. A future version
   would retrieve authoritative guidance and support professional review.

3. **No persistent client context.** Work is not retained across sessions.
   A future version would maintain separate client workspaces with
   documents, prior analyses, and approved decisions.
